You are right, after some digging, it caused by accessing Comfy via http and not https, I don't use localhost rather host on my LAN so I access via IP: 

`navigator.permissions.query({ name: "clipboard-write" }).then((result) => {
    if (result.state === "granted" || result.state === "prompt") {
        navigator.clipboard.writeText("Some text").then(() => {
            console.log("Copied successfully!");
        }).catch(err => {
            console.error("Failed to copy:", err);
        });
    } else {
        console.error("Clipboard permission denied.");
    }
});
`
The `navigator.clipboard` API only works in secure contexts (HTTPS) and in localhost.
